Description: turn reviewed test tickets into automated Playwright tests
 qualfy reads reviewed test tickets (markdown files, Jira, GitHub issues),
 validates them against a YAML contract, and hands them to an AI agent
 (Claude Code) that writes and runs Playwright tests in the target
 repository. Results are reported back as JSON files or ticket comments.
 .
 The interactive TUI needs python3-textual 2.1 or newer (Ubuntu 25.04+);
 without it qualfy falls back to plain prompts. The Claude Code CLI
 (`claude`) is not packaged and must be installed separately.
